# The list of the names that the objects of a layout may gain has two parts: the names that are stored into objects known to have the layout, which the layout lists,
# and the names that are stored through receivers nobody knows, which the program lists once. They count for a layout that says isReachedThroughUnknownReceivers.
# A text has no such list of the program, so there an object of such a layout may gain any name, and a lookup that goes past the object holds only while no object of the layout hides the member. A layout that no such store reaches goes by its own list.
